__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
data/.universes/
*.egg-info/

# The pre-edit backups. `-47`: the standing rule in docs/HANDOFF.md says these are
# "gitignored" and they were merely UNTRACKED — one `git add -A` from entering the SSOT,
# which is why "do not git add -A" had to be a separate rule propping this one up. The
# consequence the rulings care about (evidence in a .bak is not in the SSOT — cite the test,
# not the backup) is now true by construction rather than by discipline.
# tests/test_backups_are_ignored.py holds it.
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
*.bak-*

# The deliverable's build directory. Generated .tex, .aux and the engine log; the PDF that
# matters is copied out to docs/deliverable/wealth-tensor-capture.pdf and committed there.
docs/deliverable/build/
docs/deliverable/build-v2/

# Public preprint PDFs are BUILD OUTPUT of docs/deliverable/build-public.sh, regenerable
# from the committed manuscripts in one command. The copies that are actually served live
# in the miniblog repo at public/papers/, which is where the website deploys from --
# committing them here too would put the same 600KB under two SSOTs and guarantee they
# drift. The build directories were already transient; this makes the artefact match.
docs/deliverable/public/
docs/deliverable/build-public-*/
docs/deliverable/build-v2/
